{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2173-06-21 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. You came in with abdominal pain, nausea, and some diarrhea. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2173-06-21 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. I’ve had this dull, constant pain in my upper belly for about a day. It’s different from my usual G-tube site pain. Feels more like the ulcers I’ve had before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2173-06-21 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Given your history of gastric bypass and previous marginal ulcers, we need to check if it’s ulcer-related again. We’ve done some blood work and an X-ray."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2173-06-21 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. My lipase was high last time—was it high again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2173-06-21 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your lipase was elevated—186, which is about three times the upper limit. That raised concern for pancreatitis, but your symptoms and history make us also think about ulcers or bowel overgrowth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2173-06-21 12:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had dumping syndrome and bacterial overgrowth before. Could that be flaring up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2173-06-21 12:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. That’s part of our differential. The X-ray showed no free air or obstruction, which is good. But your bladder was very full—possibly contributing to discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2173-06-21 12:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t felt the urge to go. Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2173-06-21 12:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor it. No need for a catheter unless it persists. For now, we’re starting IV fluids and holding your tube feeds temporarily—bowel rest—to see if your pancreas settles down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2173-06-21 12:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my pain? It’s still pretty constant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2173-06-21 12:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We gave you dilaudid in the ER, and we’ll continue with pain meds as needed. We’re also starting a proton-pump inhibitor to protect your stomach lining, just in case it’s an ulcer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2173-06-21 18:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Your labs are stable, and your lipase has already dropped to 118. That’s a good sign. We’re still concerned about the cause, so we’ve scheduled an MRCP tomorrow to look at your pancreas and bile ducts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2173-06-21 18:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that an MRI? I’ve had those before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2173-06-21 18:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s a special MRI that focuses on the pancreas and bile system. It will help us rule out gallstones or inflammation. We’ll also give you some oral contrast through your G-tube to check for dumping syndrome."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2173-06-21 18:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it show if I have another ulcer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2173-06-21 18:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "MRCP isn’t the best for ulcers. If we’re still suspicious, we may do an EGD—a scope down through your stomach—to look directly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2173-06-22 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your MRCP results are back. Good news—your pancreas and bile ducts look completely normal. No signs of inflammation or blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2173-06-22 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not pancreatitis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2173-06-22 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Unlikely. The elevated lipase might be from your medications—fluoxetine has a small risk. But your symptoms still point to possible ulcer. We’re scheduling an EGD this afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2173-06-22 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had a few of those. Will they treat anything they find?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2173-06-22 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. If there’s an ulcer, they can cauterize it if it’s bleeding or has a lesion. We’ll also restart your tube feeds after, using a low-protein formula to avoid stressing your system."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2173-06-22 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember last time—high protein made me confused. Is that still a concern?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2173-06-22 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Your prior workup suggested a possible urea cycle issue. We’re still waiting on genetic results, but we’ll keep protein low for now to be safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2173-06-23 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi. Your EGD is done. You had a marginal ulcer near the gastric bypass site, and there was a small pigmented lesion. It’s been cauterized, so it should heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2173-06-23 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it cancerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2173-06-23 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No biopsy was taken, but the appearance wasn’t concerning. Still, we’ll repeat the EGD in 8 weeks to make sure it’s healing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2173-06-23 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief. What about my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2173-06-23 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re increasing your pantoprazole to twice daily and adding sucralfate four times a day. That helps protect the ulcer site. You’ll take the sucralfate by mouth, not through the tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2173-06-23 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Why by mouth?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2173-06-23 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Because it coats the upper stomach and esophagus better when swallowed. It helps form a protective layer over the ulcer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2173-06-23 13:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Can I restart my tube feeds now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2173-06-23 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re restarting them now—low protein NutriHep, continuous drip. We’ll monitor for nausea or pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2173-06-23 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling? Any pain or nausea since restarting feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2173-06-23 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. Pain is down to a 3. Still a little bloated, but no vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2173-06-23 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. Your labs today also look better—lipase is normal, and your kidney function is good. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow if this continues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2173-06-23 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need pain meds at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2173-06-23 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you a short course of oxycodone for breakthrough pain. But we’ll also start a bowel regimen—senna and docusate—since narcotics can cause constipation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2173-06-23 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had that before. I’ll take them as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2173-06-23 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, your fluoxetine and atenolol are continuing. No changes there. And we’ll keep rifaximin for bacterial overgrowth prevention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2173-06-23 15:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about H. pylori? Should I be tested?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2173-06-23 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "GI wants a stool antigen test, but you haven’t had a bowel movement this admission. Please follow up with them in clinic to get it done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2173-06-24 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’ve done really well overnight—no pain, tolerating feeds, vitals stable. We’re clearing you for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2173-06-24 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2173-06-24 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue pantoprazole twice daily and sucralfate four times a day by mouth. Keep using NutriHep with low protein. Take oxycodone only if needed for pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2173-06-24 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the bowel meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2173-06-24 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, senna and docusate twice daily while on oxycodone. They’ll help prevent constipation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2173-06-24 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When do I see GI again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2173-06-24 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "In 8 weeks for a repeat EGD. They’ll check how the ulcer is healing. Call sooner if you have severe pain, vomiting, or black stools."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2173-06-24 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2173-06-24 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You’ve made great progress. We’ll send all instructions to your husband. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2173-06-21 12:02:00",
    "admission_end": "2173-06-24 14:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for abdominal pain, nausea, and diarrhea following a history of Roux-en-Y gastric bypass. Initial concern for pancreatitis was raised due to elevated lipase, but MRCP showed a normal pancreas. An EGD revealed a marginal ulcer with a pigmented lesion, which was cauterized. The patient was managed with bowel rest, IV fluids, pain control, and optimized ulcer prophylaxis including increased pantoprazole and initiation of sucralfate. Tube feeds were restarted with a low-protein formula to accommodate her history of post-prandial confusion and possible urea cycle disorder. She improved clinically, tolerated feeds, and was discharged home with a plan for GI follow-up in 8 weeks for repeat EGD and continuation of medications including proton-pump inhibitors, sucralfate, and a bowel regimen due to narcotic use.",
    "problems": [
      "Gastrojejunal ulcer, unspecified as acute or chronic, without mention of hemorrhage or perforation, without mention of obstruction",
      "Postgastric surgery syndromes",
      "Bariatric surgery status",
      "Gastrostomy status",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Unspecified disorder of pancreatic internal secretion",
      "Other and unspecified postsurgical nonabsorption"
    ]
  }
}
